Z||000000||deceler8||10-21-1999||10:20 AM||||I'm fairly new to this and haven't seen this discussed, so here goes. <P>My '86 2m4 has the steel wheels (about 20 slots, 14x5.5, I believe...it came with the cheap looking Pontiac wheelcovers...and I'm wondering if there are center caps that fit these wheels and if so, where to get them.<P>The few Fieros I've seen with these type of wheels are all 13", and none of them have caps (missing, so I don't know if they fit the 14" wheel).<P>Looks like baby moons will fit and cover the hubs and lugnuts, but can't imagine they would look okay on wheels with this offset.<P>I must admit, this forum is addictive...must look at it 15 times a day.||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||10-21-1999||10:58 AM||||I occasionally come across the caps for the steel wheels. I also have a set of 14 inch turbo fins. Cheap||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||10-21-1999||12:44 PM||||I usually go to an automotive swap meet a couple times a year since I have lots of streetrod projects. You'll be amazed at all the junk and great deals you can find at these events. It's like a giant yard sale for car nuts. I see wheels, center caps, and hubcaps at these swap meets all the time. You might check with Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||10-21-1999||03:33 PM||||Hey, Tom...you got any of the caps you'd be willing to sell ?<P>As to cheap 14" alum fins, how cheap ?<P>deceler8@yahoo.com<P>And thanks again everyone.||||reg||10
